think user functions: a function is not a value (the value model stays five kinds) but lives in a small pointer table beside the bindings; its name, params, and body point into the source; a child scope copies the pointer array cheaply
think fn name p1 p2: body defines a single-expression function; call is `name arg…`, recognised only when there is no top-level arithmetic operator so a call inside arithmetic wears parentheses, like the runes; args evaluate in the caller scope, bind into a child that inherits bindings and functions for recursion; a bounded call depth is the recursion wall
think proved it — double, add, a classify built from ?: and matches, classify called per element in a fold, and a recursive factorial all hold
think folded census_control's H1 fence-count to native Rishi — a fold with a record accumulator carries the fence state, true=1 naive=4 identical to the awk seam; repointed census_control_scan.rish to the .rish seam; gate green, prove-red still fails, downstream dated_pattern green
